cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ashcroft University Endowment: tactical asset allocation study"
message: >-
  An AI agent, given a real mandate and an obligation to be audited, produced
  this study. If you cite it, cite AUDIT.md alongside it: the study's own audit
  note records which of its results are indistinguishable from zero.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: David
    family-names: Arias
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidalmeida90/endowment-agent-investment"
url: "https://davidalmeida90.github.io/endowment-agent-investment"
abstract: >-
  A five-year tactical asset allocation study for a fictional USD 850m
  university endowment, produced end to end by an AI agent working from a single
  written brief. The agent constituted an investment office of six independent
  desks, ran the Quantitative and Macro desks blind to each other, enforced a
  point-in-time data wall through a single choke point, and audited its own
  output twice before publication. Public data only, no API keys, no paywalled
  sources. The analysis window is a parameter, so the whole study reproduces on
  a different window with no other edit.
keywords:
  - agentic-ai
  - asset-allocation
  - endowment
  - point-in-time-data
  - look-ahead-bias
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-07-30"
